license: Apache-2.0
abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. Two disjoint loose 8-cycles with two isolated vertices form a Berge-P10-saturated three-uniform hypergraph on 34 vertices with 16 hyperedges, below the value 17 conjectured by English, Graber, Kirkpatrick, Methuku and Sullivan. The preprint determines the three-uniform Berge-path saturation number for all m >= 10 and n >= 2a_m + 1, with a unique extremal hypergraph at every exceptional order. A Lean proof of the counterexample family is included. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
